# SheetFlow v2 — repository-root ignore rules
#
# The Next.js app in 10_Final_Website/ carries its own .gitignore for
# framework-local artifacts. This file covers the repository as a whole so
# build output and local noise cannot be committed from any directory.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*

# Build output
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Deployment provider
.vercel/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Environment — .env.example is tracked on purpose and must stay tracked.
# Do not broaden this to `.env*`, which would swallow it.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.pem

# Test output
/coverage

.vercel

# Added by `vercel link`. `.env*` is exactly the broadening the rule above warns
# against — it matches 10_Final_Website/.env.example, which is tracked on
# purpose and is the only documentation of the app's environment contract. The
# file survives today only because it is already in the index; a fresh clone
# adding a new one would silently lose it. The negation restores the intent of
# both rules: ignore real secrets, keep the example.
.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Visual-regression captures. 93 MB of PNGs across 129 frames at the time this
# rule was written, regenerated by `npm run shots` and `capture-narrative.mjs`
# on demand. Screenshots are *evidence*, not source: they are worth keeping on
# the machine that took them and are not worth carrying in every clone forever,
# because git stores each re-capture of a 1 MB frame as a new 1 MB blob and no
# frame is ever byte-identical to the last one.
docs/_captures/

# Playwright MCP session output — traces and console logs for one browser
# session, useful while debugging it and meaningless afterwards.
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code: the project settings file is tracked on purpose (it carries the
# session-supervisor hook every contributor needs). The `.local` variant holds
# one machine's permission grants and must not be.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Config backups taken before an edit. Restore from git, not from a sibling file.
*.rc8-backup
